('037eca7b-41de-50cc-9a69-505582dde255', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '0d4f60c0-0c46-45a6-886d-ead834200dc8', 'a-level', '29.7', '9702 coursebook 29.7 · Decay graphs and equations', 44, 44, 'A detector records 450, 310, 220 and 160 counts per minute at t = 0, 5, 10 and 15 min. The background is 20 counts per minute. (a) Correct the readings for background. (b) Use the first and last corrected readings to find λ in min⁻¹. (c) Calculate the half-life in min.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '9.265', 'min', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 430, 290, 200, 140. (b) λ = ln(430 ÷ 140) ÷ 15 = 0.07481 min⁻¹. (c) t½ = 0.693 ÷ 0.07481 = 9.27 min. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: background removed. M1: ln ratio ÷ time. C1: λ. C1: t½. A1: t½ = 9.27 min.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 316" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg40ae0a18-t fg40ae0a18-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg40ae0a18-t">Raw count rates</title><desc id="fg40ae0a18-d">Table and graph of raw count rate against time: 450, 310, 220 and 160 counts per minute at 0, 5, 10 and 15 minutes, with the background of 20 counts per minute shown dashed.</desc><g transform="translate(0,0)"><rect x="29.9" y="8" width="340.2" height="56" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="29.9" y="8" width="340.2" height="28" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="105" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">t / min</text><text x="203.8" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">0</text><line x1="180" y1="8" x2="180" y2="64" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:no