('ebcdd39f-53e9-5829-9bfb-f8807e420d38', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '0d4f60c0-0c46-45a6-886d-ead834200dc8', 'a-level', '29.7', '9702 coursebook 29.7 · Decay graphs and equations', 45, 45, 'A graph of ln(A / Bq) against t (in minutes) has an intercept of 8.0 and a gradient of −0.050 min⁻¹. (a) Calculate the initial activity. (b) Calculate λ in s⁻¹. (c) Calculate the initial number of undecayed nuclei. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.577e6', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) A₀ = e^8.0 = 2981 Bq. (b) λ = 0.050 ÷ 60 = 8.333 × 10⁻⁴ s⁻¹. (c) N₀ = A₀/λ = 2981 ÷ 8.333 × 10⁻⁴ = 3.58 × 10⁶. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: A₀ from intercept. C1: min⁻¹ to s⁻¹. M1: N = A/λ. C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: N₀ = 3.58 × 10⁶.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('df83f628-3bcf-5cea-a1b5-822148a77018', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '0d4f60c0-0c46-45a6-886d-ead834200dc8', 'a-level', '29.7', '9702 coursebook 29.7 · Decay graphs and equations', 46, 46, 'A sample has an activity of 5.0 MBq at 10:00 and 3.2 MBq at 14:00. (a) Calculate λ in h⁻¹. (b) Calculate the half-life in hours.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6.213', 'h', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) λ = ln(5.0 ÷ 3.2) ÷ 4.0 = 0.1116 h⁻¹. (b) t½ = 0.693 ÷ 0.1116 = 6.21 h. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: time interval 4.0 h. M1: λ = ln(A₁/A₂)/t. C1: λ. C1: t½. A1: t½ = 6.21 h.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('225f90ab-6335-5e5e-bfcd-d37e362a67e4', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '0d4f60c0-0c46-45a6-886d-ead834200dc8', 'a-level', '29.7', '9702 coursebook 29.7 · Decay graphs and equations', 47, 47, 'The graph shows N against t for a sample. (a) Read N₀ and the half-life. (b) Calculate λ. (c) Calculate the initial activity. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.04e8', 'Bq', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) N₀ = 6.0 × 10⁹; N halves to 3.0 × 10⁹ at t = 40 s, so t½ = 40 s. (b) λ = 0.693 ÷ 40 = 0.01733 s⁻¹. (c) A₀ = 0.01733 × 6.0 × 10⁹ = 1.04 × 10⁸ Bq. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: N₀. C1: t½ from graph. C1: λ. M1: A = λN. C1: value. A1: A₀ = 1.04 × 10⁸ Bq.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg0079d5eb-t fg0079d5eb-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg0079d5eb-t">Undecayed nuclei against time</title><desc id="fg0079d5eb-d">Graph of the number of undecayed nuclei against time from 0 to 160 s: it starts at 6.0 × 10⁹ and falls exponentially, halving every 40 s.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="113.5" y1="34" x2="113.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="203" y1="34" x2="203" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="292.5" y1="34" x2="292.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-g