('b7010678-3570-5d31-9c1b-81b98b9258b0', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '0d4f60c0-0c46-45a6-886d-ead834200dc8', 'a-level', '29.7', '9702 coursebook 29.7 · Decay graphs and equations', 50, 50, 'A source decays so that ln(A / Bq) = 5.5 − 0.0693t, with t in hours. (a) State the initial activity. (b) Calculate the half-life in hours.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10', 'h', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) A₀ = e^5.5 = 245 Bq. (b) λ = 0.0693 h⁻¹, so t½ = 0.693 ÷ 0.0693 = 10.0 h. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: A₀ = e^5.5. M1: gradient = −λ. C1: λ. C1: t½. A1: t½ = 10.0 h.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('0a89e586-947d-5197-83ea-ac1ff7313550', 'aae53119-5afd-4055-b81b-60e6244772d7', '0d4f60c0-0c46-45a6-886d-ead834200dc8', 'a-level', '29.7', '9702 coursebook 29.7 · Decay graphs and equations', 51, 51, 'A sample contains two isotopes. After a long time, the graph of ln A against t becomes a straight line of gradient −0.010 s⁻¹, showing only the long-lived isotope remains. (a) Explain why the graph is curved at first. (b) Calculate the half-life of the long-lived isotope. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '69.31', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) At first both isotopes contribute; the short-lived one dies away quickly. (b) t½ = 0.693 ÷ 0.010 = 69.3 s. Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: two components. B1: short-lived decays first. M1: gradient = −λ. C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: t½ = 69.3 s.', 6, NULL, NULL)
